<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ilisu Dam</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2006–2018</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilisu">Ilisu</a> Dam is a large hydroelectric dam on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigris">Tigris</a> in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, part of the Southeastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> Project. Built between 2006 and 2018, it began filling in 2019, and by 2020 its reservoir had submerged most of the ancient town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hasankeyf">Hasankeyf</a> and dozens of villages, despite international protest. Some monuments were moved to a new site before the flooding.</p></div>
